# Enforce LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the index.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks text files out as CRLF, and two things
# in this repository are executed rather than read:
#
#   - `install.py --project --git-hook` writes `.githooks/pre-commit`, a POSIX
#     `sh` script. Under WSL or Git Bash a CRLF shebang line fails with
#     `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, which is an error message that names the
#     wrong problem and costs an hour.
#   - `templates/demo.tape` is fed to Charm VHS, which runs on Unix.
#
# CI also lints this tree on Ubuntu and macOS, so a CRLF checkout here would be
# a difference between platforms in a project whose central claim is that there
# is none.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries - never normalize, never diff as text.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated from the rule definitions by `readme_lint.py --rules`; CI fails if
# it has drifted. Marking it generated collapses it in diffs and keeps it out of
# language statistics, where it would otherwise misreport the repo as Markdown.
docs/rubric.md linguist-generated=true

# The profile READMEs and the tape are templates full of {{PLACEHOLDER}} text.
# They are documentation, not the project's own prose.
templates/** linguist-documentation=true
